<title>DENMARK: SBAB raises 4-pct 2003 bond to 400 mln DKK.</title>
<headline>SBAB raises 4-pct 2003 bond to 400 mln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish state-owned mortgage lender SBAB is raising the amount of its existing four-percent bond, due in 2003, by 200 million Danish crowns ($29.3 million) to 400 million, arranger Den Danske Bank said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Den Danske Bank took all the bonds for resale, it said.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom + 45 33969650 ($ = 6.829 Danish Crowns)</p>
</text>
